  "summary": "A threat actor exploited the Samsung MagicINFO vulnerability CVE-2025-4632 (via the Apache Tomcat service, tomcat9.exe) to install a rogue AnyDesk instance, create the local admin account 'oldadministrator', and disable Microsoft Defender. They then ran Silent XMR Miner Builder.exe on the endpoint, which spawned .NET and C compilers (csc.exe, cvtres.exe, donut.exe, tcc.exe, cc1.exe, gcc.exe) to compile a cryptominer that was injected into explorer.exe and mined Monero via the public C3Pool service.",
